ferent set of projections of the same image space. A's unit 7 is dead (zero weights, negative bias), so it carries no information.\n\n*Construction.* Inside the ReLU's active region, h1A ≈ x·W1A + b1A. I want z1B = x·W1B + b1B. So I need M with W1A·M ≈ W1B, which means re-expressing each B detector in terms of A's detectors.\n\n- **Choosing M.** The exact least-squares answer needs a 16×16 matrix inverse, which I can't do by hand. Instead I used the transpose estimator, normalised per unit: M[i,j] = ⟨wA_i, wB_j⟩ / (1.4·‖wA_i‖²).\n  - The extra factor 1.4 shrinks M a little to allow for the non-orthogonality of A's columns.\n- **Which pixels.** I computed the inner products over 16 high-variance central pixels:\n  - rows 1, 3, 4 and 6, columns 2–5\n  - weights rounded to 0.1\n\n  Border pixels are almost always blank, so their weights matter little.\n- **Choosing c.** c = b1B − b1A·M removes A's biases and inserts B's. The dead unit's row of M is zero.\n\nThis is an approximation, so B should do clearly better than the 10% of a random bridge, but well below B's own accuracy.\n\n**Bridge:**\n```json\n{\"M\": [\n[0.04,0.30,-0.39,-0.02,0.20,0.07,0.50,0.13,0.08,0.01,0.16,0.26,-0.20,-0.01,0.41,0.16,0.42,0.18,-0.28,0.34,0.33,0.16,-0.03,-0.01],\n[0.10,0.19,-0.06,-0.29,0.09,-0.14,0.50,0.01,0.27,0.33,0.03,0.30,-0.14,-0.12,0.23,0.33,0.03,0.17,0.07,-0.01,0.16,0.09,-0.04,0.15],\n[0.29,0.33,0.13,0.15,0.15,0.02,0.29,0.06,0.00,0.30,0.09,0.14,-0.04,0.19,0.17,0.39,0.04,0.23,-0.01,0.14,-0.07,0.03,-0.13,0.06],\n[-0.44,-0.28,-0.13,-0.14,0.08,0.08,0.06,-0.25,0.36,0.03,-0.01,0.29,-0.27,-0.38,-0.01,-0.04,-0.19,0.33,0.09,-0.09,0.35,-0.07,0.08,0.23],\n[0.23,0.09,0.05,-0.04,-0.18,0.02,0.00,0.18,-0.09,-0.08,0.25,-0.24,0.15,0.15,-0.11,-0.12,0.21,-0.07,-0.10,0.13,-0.12,0.11,0.10,-0.07],\n[-0.06,-0.24,-0.19,-0.13,-0.36,0.08,-0.20,0.07,0.08,-0.21,-0.18,0.08,0.20,0.24,-0.10,-0.26,-0.30,0.21,0.13,-0.29,0.11,-0.08,0.46,0.00],\n[-0.21,-0.09,-0.16,-0.32,0.10,0.10,0.25,0.08,0.38,0.04,0.30,0.16,-0.24,-0.